  "instance_name": "mapping_id_1",
  "label": "Self-identification through infantilizing text",
  "description": "The text 'the name's bob... bob' is mapped onto the visual entity of the man with Down syndrome, creating an analogical mapping where the man is portrayed as a simple, repetitive self-introduction, reinforcing the stereotype of infantilization associated with ableism. The text explicitly labels the visual subject as 'bob', reducing his identity to a simplistic, repetitive name, which is a key element of the ableist trope.",
